    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 civic has been making this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be the serpentine belt? can u explain what that belt actually does and why a bad one would make that noise?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a crucial component that transfers power from the engine's crankshaft to various accessories like the alternator, power steering pump, and A/C compressor. When this belt wears out, slips, or becomes loose, it can create a high-pitched squealing sound, especially under the load of acceleration. This noise usually signals that the belt needs to be inspected and likely replaced to prevent further mechanical issues.",
      "source": "target",
